// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes d2
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "d2.1" source="d2" target="SNOMED_CT:258156005" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source d2 SNOMED CT 258156005 = ICF chapter root for the task-execution/activity-demand domain. No
        single SNOMED CT concept denotes the ICF d2 chapter as a whole. Target (@sv: vardagsuppgifter) is
        the closest ICF-aligned observable — its name closely mirrors the chapter's task-execution scope
        and it sits in the SNOMED CT functional observable hierarchy. Broader climb from chapter root to
        observable; low tier per rubric (deeper climb, chapter-level generality).
        """
}
mapping "d210.1" source="d210" target="SNOMED_CT:716467004" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source d210 SNOMED CT 716467004 = ICF activity of carrying out a single task independently or in a
        group. Target; Swedish mirror synonym @sv: kan utföra en enstaka uppgift matches the ICF source
        name verbatim — this is an explicit ICF-aligned SNOMED CT concept. Paradigm breadth mismatch: the
        SNOMED CT finding asserts a positive capability, whereas the ICF d-code denotes the activity domain
        assessed for capacity AND performance (with or without difficulty). The target captures the
        capability aspect but is not fully co-extensive with the ICF domain; broader at high tier
        (one-level breadth mismatch, name-verified).
        """
}
mapping "d2100.1" source="d2100" target="SNOMED_CT:716467004" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source d2100 SNOMED CT 716467004 = ICF activity of carrying out a simple, uncomplicated task.
        Target (@sv: kan utföra en enstaka uppgift). SNOMED CT has no concept distinguishing from other
        single tasks, so the ICF-aligned parent finding subsumes this source. One-level broader;
        moderate tier (no distinction, paradigm breadth mismatch as in d210).
        """
}
